(PREFACE.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The produce of the earth--all that is derived from its surface by the) Tj T*
(united application of labour, machinery, and capital, is divided among) Tj T*
(three classes of the community; namely, the proprietor of the land, the) Tj T*
(owner of the stock or capital necessary for its cultivation, and the) Tj T*
(labourers by whose industry it is cultivated.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But in different stages of society, the proportions of the whole produce) Tj T*
(of the earth which will be allotted to each of these classes, under the) Tj T*
(names of rent, profit, and wages, will be essentially different;) Tj T*
(depending mainly on the actual fertility of the soil, on the) Tj T*
(accumulation of capital and population, and on the skill, ingenuity, and) Tj T*
(instruments employed in agriculture.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
